# Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters

Approach

Step 1
Create an array to store the last index of each character and initialize it with -1.

Step 2
Use two pointers (left and right) to maintain the current window.

Step 3
If the current character has already appeared inside the current window, move the left pointer to one position after its last occurrence.

Step 4
Update the last index of the current character.

Step 5
Calculate the current window length and update the maximum length.

Step 6
Continue until the right pointer reaches the end of the string.

Time Complexity
O(n)

Space Complexity
O(256) ≈ O(1)